{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/953408-price-of-mana","id":953408,"title":"Price of Mana","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-18T13:45:43-07:00","id":953408,"title":"Price of Mana","content":"Done quick search of subforum, could not found this. <b>I ask here about price range for one darm ( point ) of Mana in general <i>Mage</i> setting, putted by Libertines.</b> In my running Boston game players are going to Dread Wrens sanctum and <b>Boston Unveiled</b> says they sell Tass 'usually for around $10,000 per point of Mana (a unit called a \u201cpawn\u201d; payment must be in genuine US Mint currency and non-sequential bills)'.<br /> <br /> I must say I just made big eyes on those numbers! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Mana maybe is Supernal energy of reality, but in 2E you can really have problem with her <b><i>only</i> till you get to Legacy</b>. I was more thinking that number like $1,000, but even this seemed to me a very step price for it - maybe price range of $500 per point seems more reasonable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T14:52:05-07:00","id":953436,"title":"","content":"To get the obvious statement out the way: It depends.<br /> <br /> Mana's cost will, like any item, fluctuate with rarity. Most Mages don't need a Hallow once they join a Legacy; they can usually get enough Mana on a daily basis to supply their needs. Hence, Mana usually goes out to the relatively new Awakened, not the elder exemplars. That the elder exemplars are the types who can control a Hallow often doubles this particular point.<br /> <br /> Since Mana is readily available and can't be stored <i>too</i> long, and, indeed, must be consumed for the health of the local Hallow, I'd say a dram of Mana is pretty cheap. At the same time, demand is never zero, so there's always customers.<br /> <br /> To that end, most Mages trade Mana like you would a gym membership; not in drams, but in a &quot;You can have X in Y time period, with Z restrictions&quot;, in exchange for a specific favour or the promise of a favour within the same or a different time period. Usually, these favours are minor and not onerous but might've been otherwise politically disadvantageous; a healing spell after a fight; a vote at the Consilium. Something like that.<br /> <br /> That's the way it's been in my games, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T19:28:14-07:00","id":953583,"title":"","content":"There was a thread on this once before already, just so you know.<br /> <br /> Also, it's not the best idea to base the price of mana in 2e on an assumption that was present in 1e since the mechanics and availability of mana are completely different. Especially because many of the restrictions on gaining mana in 1e were removed in 2e. Mana is more available and as such is going to be sort of cheap, it's value lies in the immediacy of the need or the inability to get your hands on it any other way at the time.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, for Mages, money is cheap. Asking for ten grand isn't necessarily a lot of money the way it is to you and me.<br /> <br /> Axelgear probably has the best approach though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T02:14:37-07:00","id":953725,"title":"","content":"A quick rule? You need Resources 1 for 3 Mana, Resources 2 for 6, and so on. Ties in nicely with the Hallow merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T04:31:33-07:00","id":987189,"title":"","content":"So I checked some Resources 2 things prices - like <a href=\"http://www.cabelas.com/catalog/browse/pump-action-shotguns/_/N-1114871/Ns-CATEGORY_SEQ_104803380\" target=\"_blank\">shotguns</a> or <a href=\"https://www.walmart.com/browse/sports-outdoors/rifles/4125_546956_1107532_1225336_1225338\" target=\"_blank\">rifles</a> - and they seems to be in price range of circa $200 - $500. So it like 6 Mana would be Resources 2, then it would like 100$ per darm of Mana. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T10:37:24-07:00","id":987328,"title":"","content":"Great thread idea. I love this kind of fantasy economics maths, would that I knew how to calculate supply and demand properly. I do think when you're designing your Consilium, and its economy, you need to consider local Mana economy, at least a little. Hallow density, and by extension, Mana abundance, is a great way to determine the &quot;power level&quot; of an area, and which faction owns them is a crude measure of the balance of power. It's actually a plot point in my game where the Pentacle have control of the majority of Hallows in the city, and the Seers are developing magical devices to siphon Hallows via ley lines at range, and have a heightened tendency to kidnap and scour Sleepers. A setting where Pentacle mages need to pay $5,000 for a point of Mana is radically different to 50 bucks a pop, but you can conceive of both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12121-ainsoph","name":"AinSoph","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T11:15:30-07:00","id":987337,"title":"","content":"For example, it's one where the stray cat population takes a dramatic plunge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T18:19:01-07:00","id":987524,"title":"","content":"You know, it would be awesome if the great Multiplexer could write a dungeonomics article on the the economics of mana. I have no idea if she's into Mage, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T18:34:01-07:00","id":987529,"title":"","content":"1 Mana=2 chickens","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-14T19:03:08-07:00","id":987537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/953408-price-of-mana?p=987529#post987529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 Mana=2 chickens</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically it's one chicken.<br /> <br /> Mana can be gained by scouring your Pattern, you could make 3 to 9 Mana every 24 hours at Gnosis 1 if you weren't busy and were willing to be exhausted.<br /> <br /> Did you mean Tass? I think that was the one that had a price attached to it, as Mana can be channeled but isn't usually in a salable form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T13:16:34-07:00","id":987903,"title":"","content":"The Mystagogue in me is appalled at all of you for your blatant capitalism concerning a supernal mystery.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}